WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:05.572
NARRATOR: But
everyone loves Lucy.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:09.275
The story of this great white
is the classic "Finding Nemo"

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:13.780
tale, but about
2,000 pounds heavier.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:17.917
When divers spotted
Lucy back in 2008,

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:21.087
her distinctive tail
wound looked fresh.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:25.291
And she seemed in desperate
need of a good meal.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:29.996
A damaged caudal often puts
a shark's life in danger.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:33.600
It's crucial for propelling
a shark through water.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:34.934
APRYL BOYLE: Lucy's
its tail deformity

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:37.270
could be from fighting
with another shark

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.372
when she was younger.

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:44.978
NARRATOR: And Lucy's not
only survived, she's thrived.

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:49.182
She did it by modifying the way
she swims to sway a little more

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:50.450
than the average great white.

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:57.090
And now Lucy's
adoring public keeps

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.959
an eye out for her
signature floppy fin

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:03.263
and her unique swagger.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.031
Unlike other
female great whites,

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:08.501
Lucy returns to Guadalupe
Island every year.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:11.137
And that is because she
has not given birth yet.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:14.507
If she did, she'd be gone
at least 12 to 18 months,

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:18.144
because that's how long
a shark pregnancy lasts.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.746
NARRATOR: Fans
don't know for sure

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:22.749
why Lucy is still not a mom.

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:24.984
It could be that male
sharks are turned

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.653
off by her misshapen fin.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:33.326
Or maybe Lucy hasn't
yet met Zapata,

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:36.463
the most famous and
recognizable male great white

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:39.199
of Guadalupe Island.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:42.235
This tough guy is a
14-footer, who has mixed it up

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.737
with other apex
predators and has

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.507
the battle scars to prove it.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:50.076
RALPH COLLIER: Zapata
is a very large shark.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:52.579
To sustain the
wounds it received,

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:56.416
the attacking shark must have
been very large, possibly

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.852
18 or 20 feet in length.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.955
NARRATOR: He might not play
well with other sharks.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:06.559
But luckily, unlike
Bullet, Zapata actually

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.362
enjoys hanging out with people.

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:12.532
That's my favorite
shark right there, Zapata.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:20.573
NARRATOR: Scarboard, at an
intimidating 18 feet long,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.842
isn't just one of the
most massive sharks

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:25.478
at Guadalupe Island,
she's one of the biggest

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:26.980
great whites in the world.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:32.886
But like all sharks, no one
will know for sure how old

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:37.190
she is until after she dies.

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:39.893
RALPH COLLIER: One of the ways
to determine the age of a shark

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.494
is by dissecting it.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.897
If we cut through
a vertebra, we can

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:50.069
see rings similar to those of
a tree showing annual growth.

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:52.505
She got her
nautically themed name

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:56.442
because of scars on the right,
or starboard, side of her body.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.947
APRYL BOYLE: When sharks
engage in head-to-head combat,

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.550
they can do incredible
damage to each other, which

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.084
is what happened to Scarboard.

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:08.254
But sharks have amazing
healing abilities.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:12.492
NARRATOR: Scarboard shows up
at Guadalupe every other year.

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:15.862
And the next time you see
her, many of her scars

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:16.596
might be gone.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:35.915
Bullet, Lucy, Zapata,
and Scarboard,

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:40.720
four sharks whose physical
flaws grabbed our attention.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:44.057
and helped make them famous.

